Audio attribution
=================

Every voice clip in this game is a real person in a recorded English
conversation, excerpted from the Edinburgh International Accents of English
Corpus (EdAcc), University of Edinburgh:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/edinburghcstr/edacc

The EdAcc corpus is shared under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes made: short conversational turns by the same speaker were joined into
excerpts of about 10-13 seconds, loudness-normalized, and converted to mono
MP3. In line with the sharealike condition, this edited clip set is shared
under the same CC BY-SA 4.0 license. Per-clip credits are in ATTRIBUTION.md,
and the edited clips are the MP3 files in the clips/ folder of this
repository.

Answers in the game are the corpus's own accent labels for each recording.
An accent label describes speech, not where someone was born or raised.
